		<link rel="alternate" href="http://forums.postgresql.fr/viewtopic.php?pid=33176#p33176"/>
		<content type="html"><![CDATA[<p>Bonjour,</p><p>Vous devriez regarder du côté de GROUP BY et des fonctions d&#039;aggrégat :</p><br /><p>- <a href="https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/queries-table-expressions.html#QUERIES-GROUP" rel="nofollow">https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current … RIES-GROUP</a><br />- <a href="https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/sql-select.html#SQL-GROUPBY" rel="nofollow">https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current … QL-GROUPBY</a><br />- <a href="https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/functions-aggregate.html" rel="nofollow">https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current … egate.html</a></p><br /><p>Voire grouping sets si vous voulez vraiment générer la liste de total en SQL: <a href="https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/queries-table-expressions.html#QUERIES-GROUPING-SETS" rel="nofollow">https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current … UPING-SETS</a></p>]]></content>
